{
  "version": 1,
  "description": "Demo manifest. fs_secret: file contents are secret; names and metadata are not. fs_public: notes + repo working tree; files on disk are trusted, as in the Claude Code profile, so a file written while the session was tainted counts as trusted when a later session reads it (see MCP-PROXY.md to close this). fetch: both a source and a sink. git: mutations require a trusted context; status and diff match fs_public reads; log (author emails), git_show and git_branch stay internal.",
